@format 1
@id functionality.media-loading.common.list-selection
@title Media loading — common Files selection
@section Functionality
@area Media loading — Common
@entry row-press, row-release, select-all, remove-selected, clear-files
@summary Trace shared Files interactions that can publish a current path and therefore invoke a tab-specific viewer adapter.
@related functionality.media-loading.common.list-clear, functionality.media-loading.split, functionality.media-loading.edit, functionality.media-loading.convert, functionality.media-loading.audio, functionality.media-loading.merge, functionality.media-loading.funnel
@tag media
@tag loading
@tag common
@tag selection

@alias list = Cadroue.UIShell.PPanels.PList

[row-press] Files row mouse press <input>
- Apply normal, Control, or Shift selection for the pressed row @ list.PListPressHandle(...)
> row-press-publish

[row-press-publish] Press selection publication <process>
- Publish the selected current path as part of the row-selection operation @ list.PListCurrentApply(...)
> row-press-output

[row-press-output] Current path after press <output>
= The scenario-specific selected-path adapter receives the published path.

[row-release] Files row mouse release <input>
- Release a previously captured row interaction and collapse a retained multi-selection only when a collapse path is pending @ list.PListReleaseHandle(...)
> row-release-result

[row-release-result] Release outcome <decision>
- Republish the collapsed row only when the earlier press left a collapse path pending @ list.PListReleaseHandle(...)
? "Selection collapsed" > row-release-publish
? "No collapse pending" > row-release-nochange

[row-release-publish] Release selection publication <process>
- Publish the collapsed current path @ list.PListCurrentApply(...)
> row-release-output

[row-release-output] Current path after release <output>
= The scenario-specific selected-path adapter receives the republished path.

[row-release-nochange] Release changes nothing <output>
= No current-path publication occurs.

[select-all] Files Control+A <input>
- Test Control+A against the current Files selection and docket contents @ list.PListKeyHandle(...)
> select-all-result

[select-all-result] Select-all eligibility <decision>
- Apply the full selection only when Control+A, an existing selection, and at least one docket path are present @ list.PListKeyHandle(...)
  @ list.PListSelectionApply(...)
? "Eligible" > select-all-publish
? "Ineligible" > select-all-nochange

[select-all-publish] Select-all current publication <process>
- Preserve the current path when possible, otherwise publish the last selected path @ list.PListCurrentApply(...)
> select-all-output

[select-all-output] Current path after Select All <output>
= The scenario-specific selected-path adapter receives the published path.

[select-all-nochange] Select All ignored <output>
= No current-path publication occurs.

[remove-selected] Remove selected Files <input>
- Resolve the selected unlocked paths and remember the first removed index @ list.PListRemove(...)
> remove-result

[remove-result] Remove eligibility <decision>
- Continue only when at least one selected path is unlocked and removable @ list.PListRemove(...)
? "Removal performed" > remove-publish
? "Nothing removable" > remove-nochange

[remove-publish] Replacement-path publication <process>
- Remove the selected paths, allow the docket-removed subscriber to select a remaining path when necessary, then publish the clamped replacement selected by the direct Remove command @ list.PListDocketRemoveHandle(...)
  @ list.PListRemove(...)
! A direct Remove can synchronously publish one replacement during the docket-removed callback and then publish the clamped replacement immediately afterward; the later request can supersede the first.
> remove-output

[remove-output] Current path after removal <output>
= A remaining path can be published to the scenario-specific selected-path adapter; an empty docket publishes no media path.

[remove-nochange] Removal ignored <output>
= The Files current path is unchanged.
[clear-files] Remove all Files button <input>
- Invoke the registered Remove All callback from the list-button click and enter the shared PListClear path @ list.PListButtonBuild(...)
> map:functionality.media-loading.common.list-clear
